From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: ntdll: a battery that reports energy reads right

The Linux battery state read only charge_full, charge_now and current_now
(uAh, uA). Many batteries -- ThinkPads among them -- report energy_full,
energy_now and power_now (uWh, uW) instead: they read as having no capacity
(GetSystemPowerStatus: 100%, "high", no time left), so the taskbar's
battery icon and every program saw nothing useful. The energy files are
used when there is no charge. Gate: make test-battery.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -3979,6 +3979,15 @@
                 bs->MaxCapacity = get_sys_int(path, "charge_full") * voltage / 1e9;
                 bs->RemainingCapacity = get_sys_int(path, "charge_now") * voltage / 1e9;
                 bs->Rate = -get_sys_int(path, "current_now") * voltage / 1e9;
+                /* Stained Glass OS: many batteries (ThinkPads among them) report
+                 * energy (uWh, uW) instead of charge (uAh, uA): there is then no
+                 * charge_full, and the battery read as empty of capacity. */
+                if (!bs->MaxCapacity && get_sys_int(path, "energy_full") > 0)
+                {
+                    bs->MaxCapacity = get_sys_int(path, "energy_full") / 1000;
+                    bs->RemainingCapacity = get_sys_int(path, "energy_now") / 1000;
+                    bs->Rate = -get_sys_int(path, "power_now") / 1000;
+                }
                 if (!bs->Charging && (LONG)bs->Rate < 0)
                     bs->EstimatedTime = 3600 * bs->RemainingCapacity / -(LONG)bs->Rate;
                 else
